# Autocomplete-Only Copilot Integration

This fork has one product surface: GitHub Copilot inline autocomplete inside the Obsidian editor.

## Keep

- `CopilotAgent`: starts and stops the Copilot language server process.
- `Client`: owns JSON-RPC/LSP communication.
- `EventManager` and `EventListener`: keep the active Markdown document synced and request inline completions.
- `InlineSuggestion*`: render ghost text, accept/cancel/cycle suggestions, and keep arrow-first keyboard behavior.
- `CopilotPluginSettingTab` and `AuthModal`: provide Node path, performance settings, sign-in, and sign-out.

## Avoid

- Do not add chat, conversation history, model pickers, prompt settings, markdown rendering, or React UI.
- Do not make `Tab` the primary accept key.
- Do not add broad compatibility shims unless the current Obsidian autocomplete path needs them.

## Interaction Contract

- `Right Arrow`: accept full suggestion.
- `Alt-Right`: accept next word.
- `Alt-ArrowDown` / `Alt-ArrowUp`: cycle suggestions.
- `Escape`: dismiss suggestion.
- Optional configured hotkeys are secondary bindings only.
